    {
      "id": "W0_YtWHaMzaUW37anLiNl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2283.862471713178,
      "y": 1027.887991684948,
      "width": 324.4317321777344,
      "height": 840,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bMqKZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 285633772,
      "version": 2127,
      "versionNonce": 487706988,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1772434205302,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Have daily and weekly session targets by\ndefault have 1 daily and 2 weekly whic.\n\nOn the active days section, have them\nmarked with rectangles\nBy default have active in all days. When\na date is tapped goes throught the\nfollowing states\n\nactive (reprepsented as full rectangle) ->\nNot active (repr as blank)-> Only active\non mornings (have a rectangle on the\nupper part of the rectangle) -> Middle of\nday only (active only on middle) -> Night\nactive (only active at night) On the right\nside wuld be indicatitn on small text\nlogically what was selected since on the\nrectangles it wont say which is monday,\nsaturday, just the icon representations.\n(starting the first rectangle as Monday,\nthen Tuesday, etc)\n\nOn the work Hours Settings have the\ndefined per heach on 24 hours format\nthe hour and minute where the mornign\nafternoon, evening starts by default\nhave some standard values that the user\ncan edit\n\nAnd also on the right side have the\noptions checkbox such as whether to\nsend notification, show the box only\nproject as selectionable chip only when\nwithin an hour of the target. And have a\ndont score project if outside the horu\nrange.\n\n\nAt last have the session duration where\nthe quick access buttons to increase and\ndecreases On the plus and minus button\nincrease on 5 to 5 intervals",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "Lf3rwx0dJY8xurW4djxzR",
      "originalText": "Have daily and weekly session targets by default have 1 daily and 2 weekly whic.\n\nOn the active days section, have them marked with rectangles\nBy default have active in all days. When a date is tapped goes throught the following states\n\nactive (reprepsented as full rectangle) -> Not active (repr as blank)-> Only active on mornings (have a rectangle on the upper part of the rectangle) -> Middle of day only (active only on middle) -> Night active (only active at night) On the right side wuld be indicatitn on small text logically what was selected since on the rectangles it wont say which is monday, saturday, just the icon representations. (starting the first rectangle as Monday, then Tuesday, etc)\n\nOn the work Hours Settings have the defined per heach on 24 hours format the hour and minute where the mornign afternoon, evening starts by default have some standard values that the user can edit\n\nAnd also on the right side have the options checkbox such as whether to send notification, show the box only project as selectionable chip only when within an hour of the target. And have a dont score project if outside the horu range.\n\n\nAt last have the session duration where the quick access buttons to increase and decreases On the plus and minus button increase on 5 to 5 intervals",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
