    {
      "id": "iS0v6--1B2Qh8DNokblDV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1425.3501181833278,
      "y": 966.938124163471,
      "width": 253.32778930664062,
      "height": 520,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bMqKb",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1332769132,
      "version": 1586,
      "versionNonce": 747105900,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1772433789006,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Tkae similar concept and styling\nthan the room management\nscreen, similarly only the Project\nscreen unshadowed floating\nbutton when not on session.\n\nHave random option to select a\nrandomproject that is not none,\nhave the first project as no\nproject. Have a icon button to\ngo into the no-project and also\nwhen exiting a project was\nselected it should have that\nproject active. \n\nInstead of volume have\nbreakdown which are going to be\ncolored in either green or red as\nfollows:\n\nEvery Math.ceil(work time/5)\ncolor one rectangle red and then\nevery Math.ceil(break/5) color\none green. For example a 25 5\nwork break is 5 reds 1 green. \n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "Hp2KfH7OL0xKidTCWO8Vn",
      "originalText": "Tkae similar concept and styling than the room management screen, similarly only the Project screen unshadowed floating button when not on session.\n\nHave random option to select a randomproject that is not none, have the first project as no project. Have a icon button to go into the no-project and also when exiting a project was selected it should have that project active. \n\nInstead of volume have breakdown which are going to be colored in either green or red as follows:\n\nEvery Math.ceil(work time/5) color one rectangle red and then every Math.ceil(break/5) color one green. For example a 25 5 work break is 5 reds 1 green. \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
